WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.499
"Are Large Weekly Doses of Vitamin B12 Safe?"

00:00:07.169 --> 00:00:09.520
Serious adverse effects,
even with high doses

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.040
of injected vitamin B12
(hydroxocobalamin),

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.640
have never been reported.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.040
However, some patients
do report acne breakouts

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.160
after high-dose injections,
which I talked about before.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.840
But, hold on.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:22.960
When you look
at the relationship

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.400
between B12 concentrations
in the blood and mortality,

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.080
you see graphs like this,

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.000
where having low levels
isn’t good,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.200
with higher mortality,

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.960
but high levels in the blood
is associated

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.120
with higher mortality too.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.920
What are some of the ways
we could get high B12 levels?

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.920
One could be
B12 supplementation,

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.320
but it could also be due to B12
being released

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.440
from damaged tissues
or not clearing as well

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:46.800
from malfunctioning kidneys-

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.360
in other words,
reverse causation.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.520
Instead of high B12
causing disease,

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.760
disease is causing high B12.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.840
How could we tease that out?

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.120
There is a correlation between
high blood B12 and cancer,

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.240
for example.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.400
Which one might be leading
to the other?

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.160
Well, when you treat
the cancer,

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:07.520
when you shrink the tumors,
B12 levels drop,

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.200
suggesting that
the active tumor

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.440
was the source
of high vitamin B12 levels

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.840
in the circulation
instead of vice versa.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.880
And that’s what you see

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.560
when you look
at other conditions:

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.480
the blood
B12 concentrations rise

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:21.680
as a consequence
of acute and chronic illness.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:22.960
A cause-and-effect relationship

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.800
between serum
B12 concentrations

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.880
and subsequent disease
or mortality

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.960
has never been demonstrated.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.280
In fact, how else can you get
lots of B12 in your system?

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.800
By eating lots of meat.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.520
So, high B12 levels
may be a proxy in some cases

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.840
for increased intake of meat.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.440
If you go back
and separate out the effects

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.200
of different sources of B12,

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.840
high intake of vitamin B12
in the form of supplements

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.720
was not associated with any
adverse effect on mortality

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.880
and, therefore, can be regarded
as safe.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.720
And you see the same thing
when you look at the origin

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.280
of vitamin B12 levels
and mortality across the board

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.360
in a systematic review
and meta-analysis

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:58.720
of all such studies.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.520
High blood concentrations
caused by dietary sources

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.400
of vitamin B12-meat,
eggs, and dairy-

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.320
may increase
all-cause mortality,

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:09.200
but when B12 levels are high
from supplement sources,

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.040
there doesn’t seem
to be a problem,

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.320
while higher mortality

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:13.760
associated
with cardiovascular disease

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.760
or obesity is associated
with higher intake

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.600
of foods like meat.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.320
The bottom line
is that long-term studies

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:21.920
clearly indicate that treatment

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.960
with even high
pharmacological doses of B12

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.760
and the corresponding increase
in serum B12 levels

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.480
do not increase mortality risk.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.880
"Supplemental forms of B12
are considered safe

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.920
and there is no evidence-based
Tolerable Upper Intake Level

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.120
for vitamin B12,"

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.720
because you just poop out
whatever you don’t absorb.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.800
Remember, when you take
a single weekly megadose

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.320
of 2,000 micrograms of B12,

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.960
you only absorb
about 20 micrograms of it,

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:51.120
and the other 1,980 just get
flushed down the toilet.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.960
But wait, before that happens,

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:55.920
that massive load of B12
hits our colon.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.040
Might that be mucking
with our microbiome?

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.800
You think we need B12?

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.160
We only need it
for two enzymes,

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.640
whereas it’s required
for more than a dozen enzymes

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.000
in bacteria.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.400
Only a minority
of the bacteria in our gut

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.440
may make it though,
yet the vast majority need it.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.800
So, where do they get it?

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.480
They borrow it from a neighbor,

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.600
like going next door to get
a cup of flour or something.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.320
We may have a thousand or more
difference species in our gut

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:21.680
and they share vitamins.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.640
It’s like one big open bazaar
down there.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:27.520
This is just to say that B12
is a big deal for bacteria

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.960
and may play
an unrecognized role

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:30.400
in shaping the structure
and function

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.480
of our microbiome.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.960
Okay, but for good or for ill?

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:37.600
Vitamin B12 supplements
typically contain doses

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:39.120
that far exceed anything

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.680
we would naturally have seen
evolutionarily

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.440
and though it’s considered safe,

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:46.400
we know our gut bugs are
fighting over it all the time.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.160
To what extent might
excessive levels affect us?

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.080
If mice are given
the human equivalent

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.320
of just 5,000 micrograms,

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:57.600
not much seems to happen
to their microbiomes.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.640
But if they’re given
the equivalent

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:01.120
of 25,000 micrograms a day,

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.520
it accelerates the colonization
of a bad bug

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:06.160
called Citrobacter rodentium,

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:10.080
but as its name suggests,
it’s a mouse-specific pathogen.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.800
It’s not a bug
you even see in humans.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.720
But what about B12 in people?

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.720
To date, very few studies
have been done,

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.040
so the impact of vitamin B12
on our gut microbiome

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.280
has not been established.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.680
And the studies we do have
are all over the place.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.200
In this one,
B12 supplementation

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.160
in an in vitro
colonic stimulation-

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.440
basically, human feces

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.440
passed through a series
of beakers and tubes-

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.960
the B12 seemed to actually have
microbiome benefits.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.880
Other similar-type studies
showed that B12

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:38.640
seemed to have
a more limited impact

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:41.360
not affecting bacterial growth,
richness, diversity,

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.960
or total metabolite production.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:45.120
However, there was an increase
in propionate,

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.080
which is a beneficial
short-chain fatty acid.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.080
In this study,
some beneficial bacteria

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.760
that produce
short-chain fatty acids

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:54.080
were reduced by B12,
but overall,

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.880
the amount of short-chain
fatty acids went up.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.400
So, vitamin B12 supplementation

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.000
may actually be beneficial
for the gut

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.920
through interactions
with our microbiome.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:05.760
So, while B12 injections are
often used for B12 deficiency,

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.000
those individuals
may be missing out

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:12.560
on microbiome benefits
of oral supplementation.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:14.240
If anything, the potential risk

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:18.080
of giving larger weekly doses
versus smaller daily doses

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:21.280
would not be
from getting too much,

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.520
but from getting too little.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:26.160
We’re counting on
that approximate 1% absorption

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.360
at higher doses,

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.960
however this passive absorption
may vary between individuals,

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:34.560
so if we instead only absorbed
half a percent

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.400
or a tenth of a percent,

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.760
we wouldn’t get enough dosing
once a week.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.840
To boost absorption,
we can take high doses

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.520
on an empty stomach.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:44.960
Instead of passively absorbing

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:47.280
about 1%
of a 500-microgram dose

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.520
when taken with a meal,
absorption is boosted

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:52.400
by about 60%
on an empty stomach.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.080
Although the higher
weekly doses

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.160
have been proven
to improve B12 status

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.600
in deficient populations,

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.680
since we really don’t know
the long-term effects

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.600
of all that extra B12
hitting our colon,

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:02.800
an alternative would be

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:05.520
to get 2 or 2.5 micrograms
at each meal,

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.520
as I talked about
with fortified foods

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:09.762
in the last video.

